  "description": "Reid eTrail 1 500W | Electric mountain bike\nTrail-ready control. Electric assistance.\nThe Reid eTrail 1 is an electric mountain bike designed for off-road trails and varied terrain. Its alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 672Wh battery for a clean finish and balanced handling. The long, low and slack geometry is paired with an SR Suntour suspension fork with 100mm of travel, helping absorb impacts from roots, rocks and uneven ground.\nPowered by an Ananda 500W rear hub motor, the eTrail 1 provides electric assistance for climbs and changing terrain. The integrated 48V 14Ah battery supports your rides, while the Ananda D19 handlebar-mounted display provides key ride information, Bluetooth connectivity and app compatibility.\nThe drivetrain combines L-TWOO 8-speed shifters with a Shimano TX800 rear derailleur and a Shimano 12–32T freewheel. This gearing offers a practical range for different gradients and trail conditions. Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors provide controlled, consistent braking across varied riding conditions.\nLarge 29-inch wheels fitted with 2.25-inch MTB tyres provide traction, stability and rollover capability on uneven trails. A 740mm alloy riser handlebar with a 25mm rise support responsive handling, while the MTB comfort saddle and ergonomic rubber grips help maintain comfort on longer rides.\nThe Reid eTrail 1 is ideal for:\n\nOff-road riding – A trail-focused frame and geometry for varied terrain\n\nTrail comfort – SR Suntour fork with 100mm of suspension travel\n\nElectric assistance – 500W rear hub motor for climbs and changing terrain\n\nConnected riding – Ananda D19 display with Bluetooth and app compatibility\n\nVersatile gearing – L-TWOO 8-speed shifters and Shimano rear derailleur\n\nControlled braking – Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors front and rear\n\nTrail traction – 29-inch wheels with 2.25-inch tyres for grip and stability\n\nResponsive handling – Wide 740mm riser bars and a 50mm stem\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
